add(('2026', 'Apr', '2026-04-02', 2), 'prot', 'Identify the correct pair having amino acid (A) and the hormone (B) that is iodinated derivative of the amino acid (A). (T and Y represent one letter code for amino acids)', ['A: T, B: Insulin', 'A: T, B: Thyroxine', 'A: Y, B: Thyroxine', 'A: Y, B: Insulin'], 3,
    lambda: pick([('Thr', 'insulin'), ('Thr', 'thyroxine'), ('Tyr', 'thyroxine'), ('Tyr', 'insulin')], ({'T': 'Thr', 'Y': 'Tyr'}['Y'], 'thyroxine')), ['Thyroxine is made in the thyroid by iodinating TYROSINE (one-letter code Y; T is threonine).', 'Insulin is a polypeptide, not an iodinated amino acid.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2024', 'Apr', '2024-04-09', 1), 'prot', 'Total number of essential amino acid among the given list of amino acids is ______: Arginine, Phenylalanine, Aspartic acid, Cysteine, Histidine, Valine, Proline', None, 4,
    lambda: sum(1 for a in ('arginine', 'phenylalanine', 'aspartic acid', 'cysteine', 'histidine', 'valine', 'proline') if a in ESS), ['Essential (NCERT): valine, leucine, isoleucine, phenylalanine, tryptophan, threonine, methionine, lysine, arginine, histidine.', 'From the list: arginine, phenylalanine, histidine, valine → 4.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2025', 'Jan', '2025-01-29', 2), 'prot', 'Identify the essential amino acids from below : (A) Valine (B) Proline (C) Lysine (D) Threonine (E) Tyrosine', ['(C), (D) and (E) only', '(B), (C) and (E) only', '(A), (C) and (D) only', '(A), (C) and (E) only'], 3,
    lambda: pickset(['(C), (D) and (E) only', '(B), (C) and (E) only', '(A), (C) and (D) only', '(A), (C) and (E) only'], {k: n in ESS for k, n in zip('ABCDE', ('valine', 'proline', 'lysine', 'threonine', 'tyrosine'))}),
    ['Valine, lysine, threonine must come from food.', 'Proline is made in the body; tyrosine is made from phenylalanine.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2026', 'Jan', '2026-01-21', 1), 'prot', 'Identify the correct statements. A. Arginine and Tryptophan are essential amino acids. B. Histidine does not contain heterocyclic ring in its structure. C. Proline is a six membered cyclic ring amino acid. D. Glycine does not have chiral centre. E. Cysteine has characteristic feature of side chain as MeS–CH_{2}–CH_{2}–.', ['C and E Only', 'B and E Only', 'C and D Only', 'A and D Only'], 4,
    lambda: pickset(['C and E Only', 'B and E Only', 'C and D Only', 'A and D Only'], dict(A='arginine' in ESS and 'tryptophan' in ESS, B=False, C=False, D=True, E=False)),
    ['A true. B false: histidine carries an imidazole ring. C false: proline\'s ring (pyrrolidine) is FIVE-membered.', 'D true (R = H). E false: CH_{3}S–CH_{2}CH_{2}– is methionine; cysteine has HS–CH_{2}–.'], 'prot', 2)
add(('2026', 'Apr', '2026-04-04', 1), 'prot', 'Match the LIST-I (Name of amino acid) with LIST-II (One letter symbol/type): A. Arginine B. Aspartic acid C. Lysine D. Glutamic acid; I. D/Non-essential II. R/Essential III. E/Non-essential IV. K/Essential',
    ['A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III', 'A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I', 'A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II', 'A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III'], 1,
    lambda: rom(', '.join(f'{k}-{ {("R", True): "II", ("D", False): "I", ("K", True): "IV", ("E", False): "III"}[(c, n in ESS)]}' for k, n, c in zip('ABCD', ('arginine', 'aspartic acid', 'lysine', 'glutamic acid'), 'RDKE')),
                ['A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III', 'A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I', 'A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II', 'A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III']),
    ['One-letter codes: Arg R, Asp D, Lys K, Glu E.', 'Arg and Lys are essential; Asp and Glu are non-essential → A-II, B-I, C-IV, D-III.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2025', 'Jan', '2025-01-23', 2), 'prot', 'The α-Helix and β-Pleated sheet structures of protein are associated with its :', ['secondary structure', 'primary structure', 'tertiary structure', 'quaternary structure'], 1,
    lambda: pick(['secondary', 'primary', 'tertiary', 'quaternary'], 'secondary'), ['Secondary structure = local shape held by C=O···H–N hydrogen bonds: α-helix and β-pleated sheet.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2026', 'Apr', '2026-04-05', 2), 'prot', 'Identify the incorrect statement about tertiary structure of proteins.', ['They can be fibrous or globular in structure.', 'The main forces that stabilize the structure are hydrogen bonding, disulphide links, van der Waals and electrostatic forces of attraction.', 'The structure remains intact when exposed to pH changes.', 'A linear polypeptide chain will convert to a secondary structure and then further folding of the secondary structure will convert to tertiary structure.'], 3,
    lambda: pick([True, True, False, True], False), ['pH change alters charges on side chains, breaking salt bridges and H-bonds → the tertiary fold is lost (denaturation).', 'So "remains intact" is wrong; the other three describe tertiary structure correctly.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-29', 1), 'prot', 'Type of amino acids obtained by hydrolysis of proteins is :', ['β', 'α', 'δ', 'γ'], 2,
    lambda: pick(['β', 'α', 'δ', 'γ'], 'α'), ['In proteins –NH_{2} and –COOH sit on the same (α) carbon: hydrolysis gives α-amino acids.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-29', 1), 'prot', 'Number of compounds among the following which contain sulphur as heteroatom is: Furan, Thiophene, Pyridine, Pyrrole, Cysteine, Tyrosine', None, 2,
    lambda: sum(1 for f in ('C4H4O', 'C4H4S', 'C5H5N', 'C4H5N', 'C3H7NO2S', 'C9H11NO3') if atoms(f, 'S')), ['Furan has O, pyridine and pyrrole have N, tyrosine has no S.', 'Sulphur: thiophene (C_{4}H_{4}S) and cysteine (–CH_{2}SH) → 2.'], 'prot', 1)
add(('2026', 'Apr', '2026-04-08', 2), 'prot', 'Which of the following amino acid will give violet coloured complex with neutral ferric chloride solution?', ['Threonine', 'Serine', 'Tyrosine', 'Tryptophan'], 3,
    lambda: pick([False, False, True, False], True), ['Neutral FeCl_{3} gives violet with a PHENOL (Ar–OH).', 'Only tyrosine has a phenolic –OH; threonine/serine have alcoholic –OH.'], 'prot', 1)

# ---------------- nucleic acids ----------------
add(('2024', 'Feb', '2024-02-01', 1), 'nucl', 'If one strand of a DNA has the sequence ATGCTTCA, sequence of the bases in complementary strand is:', ['CATTAGCT', 'TACGAAGT', 'GTACTTAC', 'ATGCGACT'], 2,
    lambda: pick(['CATTAGCT', 'TACGAAGT', 'GTACTTAC', 'ATGCGACT'], comp('ATGCTTCA')), ['Pairing rules: A–T, G–C.', 'ATGCTTCA → TACGAAGT.'], 'nucl', 1)
add(('2025', 'Apr', '2025-04-04', 1), 'nucl', "The total number of hydrogen bonds of a DNA double helix whose one strand has the following sequence of bases is ___________: 5'-G G C A A A T C G G C T A-3'", None, 33,
    lambda: sum(HB[b] for b in 'GGCAAATCGGCTA'), ['G≡C pairs have 3 H-bonds, A=T pairs have 2.', 'G/C count = 7 → 21; A/T count = 6 → 12. Total 33.'], 'nucl', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-27', 1), 'nucl', 'Two nucleotides are joined together by a linkage known as :', ['Phosphodiester linkage', 'Glycosidic linkage', 'Disulphide linkage', 'Peptide linkage'], 1,
    lambda: pick(['phosphodiester', 'glycosidic', 'disulphide', 'peptide'], 'phosphodiester'), ['The phosphate links C5′ of one sugar to C3′ of the next: a phosphodiester bond.', 'The glycosidic bond joins base to sugar inside ONE nucleotide.'], 'nucl', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-30', 2), 'nucl', 'The total number of correct statements, regarding the nucleic acids is _______. A. RNA is regarded as the reserve of genetic information. B. DNA molecule self-duplicates during cell division. C. DNA synthesizes proteins in the cell. D. The message for the synthesis of particular proteins is present in DNA. E. Identical DNA strands are transferred to daughter cells.', None, 3,
    lambda: sum([False, True, False, True, True]), ['DNA (not RNA) is the reserve of genetic information (A false); RNA, not DNA, carries out protein synthesis (C false).', 'B, D, E are correct → 3.'], 'nucl', 1)

# ---------------- vitamins ----------------
add(('2025', 'Apr', '2025-04-03', 2), 'vit', 'Fat soluble vitamins are: A. Vitamin B_{1} B. Vitamin C C. Vitamin E D. Vitamin B_{12} E. Vitamin K', ['A & B Only', 'B & C Only', 'C & D Only', 'C & E Only'], 4,
    lambda: pickset(['A & B Only', 'B & C Only', 'C & D Only', 'C & E Only'], {k: v in FAT for k, v in zip('ABCDE', ('B1', 'C', 'E', 'B12', 'K'))}), ['Fat soluble: A, D, E, K. B-group and C are water soluble.', 'From the list: vitamin E (C) and vitamin K (E).'], 'vit', 1)
add(('2026', 'Apr', '2026-04-02', 1), 'vit', 'Match List - I (Vitamin) with List - II (Name): A. Vitamin B_{1} B. Vitamin B_{2} C. Vitamin B_{6} D. Vitamin C; I. Pyridoxine II. Ascorbic acid III. Thiamine IV. Riboflavin',
    ['A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV', 'A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I', 'A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II', 'A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV'], 3,
    lambda: rom(', '.join(f'{k}-{ {"pyridoxine": "I", "ascorbic acid": "II", "thiamine": "III", "riboflavin": "IV"}[VNAME[v]]}' for k, v in zip('ABCD', ('B1', 'B2', 'B6', 'C'))),
                ['A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV', 'A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I', 'A-III, B-IV, C-I, D-II', 'A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV']),
    ['B_{1} thiamine, B_{2} riboflavin, B_{6} pyridoxine, C ascorbic acid.'], 'vit', 1)
add(('2025', 'Jan', '2025-01-22', 1), 'vit', 'Which of the following acids is a vitamin?', ['Adipic acid', 'Aspartic acid', 'Saccharic acid', 'Ascorbic acid'], 4,
    lambda: pick(['adipic acid', 'aspartic acid', 'saccharic acid', 'ascorbic acid'], VNAME['C']), ['Ascorbic acid is vitamin C. Adipic acid → nylon-6,6; aspartic acid is an amino acid; saccharic acid comes from oxidising glucose.'], 'vit', 1)
add(('2024', 'Jan', '2024-01-31', 2), 'vit', 'From the vitamins A, B_{1}, B_{6}, B_{12}, C, D, E and K, the number of vitamins that can be stored in our body is _____.', None, 5,
    lambda: sum(1 for v in ('A', 'B1', 'B6', 'B12', 'C', 'D', 'E', 'K') if v in FAT or v == 'B12'), ['Fat-soluble vitamins (A, D, E, K) are stored in liver and adipose tissue.', 'Of the water-soluble ones only B_{12} is stored (in the liver). Total 5.'], 'vit', 1)

